DESCRIPTION:Day 3 of 3: Continental Art\, Antiques & Silver | Impressionis
 t Art | European Modern Art & Design - Featuring a strong collection of C
 ontinental art and antiques\, including a large Romanesque limestone figu
 re\, a Sienese School painting of Mary Magdalene\, Styrian School carving
 s\, Albrecht Dürer woodcuts\, and a Biedermeier secrétaire à abattant.
  Impressionist and Modern art selections feature Georges d'Espagnat from 
 the Roy E. Disney Family Collection and a John Marin watercolor from the 
 Collection of June and Frank Barsalona. An exemplary offering of Continen
 tal furniture and design features an André Ducuing lacquer screen\, a Lo
 uis XV Revival salon suite from Stevens Institute of Technology\, and an 
 Art Nouveau leaded glass screen. Additional highlights include a monument
 al Pierre Bourdelle mural from the Great Hall of the university's Samuel 
 C. Williams Library. Also featured are Art Nouveau brooches from the Esta
 te of Alexander Dobkin\, Austro-Hungarian gold cigarette cases\, and art 
 glass by Daum\, Gallé\, and Le Verre Français. The sale concludes with 
 a selection of antiquities\, including Roman glass\, Hellenistic pottery\
 , and a Gandharan schist Bodhisattva.
